Althane is the most populous realm in the [[Phenomena/Crystal Sphere|Crystal Sphere]] and is home to the greatest diversity of inhabitant races. The surface is 32% land, the majority of which is concentrated in a single supercontinent that stretches from near the planet's southern pole up past its equator. The terrain on the planet varies from jungles and deserts at the northern tip to frozen tundras in the south; with mountain ranges, temperate forests, expansive marshlands, and an inland lake large enough to support navies and maritime trade.

Althane was tidally locked with its twin [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]], and as such did not rotate about its poles, but instead orbited around a central point between the paired worlds; Ilkyne took up a large part of the sky and was always visible. Ilkyne was destroyed when [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] struck it, and is gone from the sky; the twelve realms orbit Althane alone.

![Map of Althane](maps/althane.jpg)

Beneath the surface, a network of caverns called [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/index|the Hollow]] reaches under most of the continent, holding ruins and creatures older than those above.

Althane is cut off from the rest of [[Geography/index|the Astra]] more completely than it once was, when its isolation was hidden rather than real. [[Phenomena/Althane/The Lighthouse|The Lighthouse]] holds the world apart so that no god can take it, and its anchorways are the only way a traveler leaves. [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]] is the one god-like being left inside it.
